644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nAmaretta's birthday is July 27, and her brother Enzo's birthday is September 3. Every year, Amaretta and Enzo celebrate by eating cake every day from Amaretta's birthday through Enzo's birthday (including both birthdays). If they did this for the first time in 2008, how many cake-eating days will they have observed by the end of 2016?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"ca99ff39019e3fab30e18855d5fd8cbd853e5f71887d23cc4c7ccc1a6167d088"},"seconds":18.348894596099854,"seed":743640736206309814,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we need to calculate the number of cake-eating days from Amaretta's birthday (July 27) through Enzo's birthday (September 3), inclusive, for each year from 2008 to 2016. Then, we will sum these days for each year.\n\nFirst, let's determine the number of cake-eating days in one year:\n- From July 27 to July 31: \\(31 - 27 + 1 = 5\\) days\n- For August: \\(31\\) days\n- From September 1 to September 3: \\(3\\) days\n\nAdding these together, we get:\n\\[ 5 + 31 + 3 = 39 \\text{ days} \\]\n\nThis number of days (39) is the same for each year from 2008 to 2016 because the dates of the birthdays do not change relative to the calendar.\n\nNow, we need to calculate the total number of cake-eating days over the 9 years from 2008 to 2016:\n\\[ 39 \\text{ days/year} \\times 9 \\text{ years} = 351 \\text{ days} \\]\n\nThus, the total number of cake-eating days observed by the end of 2016 is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{351}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{351}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
